# Whole feature

Before building, answer each of these in the plan. Social features (friends, family, Did you, Did we, links) must answer all of them. Template: `docs/feature-checklist.md`.

- Already friends? Not friends?
- Blocked, either way?
- Same family?
- They remove you, or leave the family?
- Signed out?
- Brand new install (link opened before onboarding)?
- Offline?
- Full or capped?
- Expired?
- What does the OTHER person see?
- What does the widget show? iOS `widgets/DidITonightWidget.tsx` and Android `widgets/android/` only draw a question that has a matching item.
- Which push goes out, and which notification switch turns it off?
- What happens to the data when the relationship ends?

## Every action says so

- Server action succeeds: `confirmDone` (`native/lib/confirm.js`) or visible inline text.
- Server action fails: `confirmMiss` or inline text. No silent no-op.
- Destructive: a `publishSheet` confirm (SheetHost) or an undo.
- Double taps: `once()` or a busy state.
- `scripts/check.mjs` enforces the "says so" part.

## Edges

- Empty states say what to do next.
- New routes go in `ROUTES` and have a way in and a way back.
- Copy buttons where the app already has them (links, codes).
